---
import GuideLayout from '../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
const locale = 'en' as const;
---
<GuideLayout
  locale={locale}
  canonicalPath="/guides/water-consumption-comparison/"
  guideTitle="Water Consumption Comparison"
  title="Water Consumption Comparison — Commercial Bakery Dishwashers"
  description="How much water does a commercial dishwasher use? Side-by-side L-per-cycle comparison of JD-3, Hobart AMX, Jackson, CMA, Winterhalter, and manual sink washing."
>
  <h1 class="mb-4">Water Consumption Comparison</h1>
  <p class="text-lg text-bakery-navy/80 mb-8">Water cost and consumption matter — for utility bills, sustainability reporting, and operating in water-stressed regions like the Middle East, Australia, and parts of the US Southwest.</p>

  <h2 class="mb-3">Per-Cycle Water Consumption</h2>
  <table class="w-full text-sm">
    <thead class="bg-bakery-navy text-white">
      <tr><th class="p-3 text-left">Machine / Method</th><th class="p-3 text-left">L per cycle</th><th class="p-3 text-left">L per 50 cycles/day</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td class="p-3 border-b font-semibold">V-TAI JD-3</td><td class="p-3 border-b">2.5</td><td class="p-3 border-b">125 L</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="p-3 border-b">Winterhalter UC-M</td><td class="p-3 border-b">2.4</td><td class="p-3 border-b">120 L</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="p-3 border-b">Hobart AMX</td><td class="p-3 border-b">3.8</td><td class="p-3 border-b">190 L</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="p-3 border-b">Jackson TempStar HH-E</td><td class="p-3 border-b">3.0</td><td class="p-3 border-b">150 L</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="p-3 border-b">CMA L-1X16-BW</td><td class="p-3 border-b">4.0</td><td class="p-3 border-b">200 L</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="p-3 border-b">Champion EHS-2</td><td class="p-3 border-b">3.5</td><td class="p-3 border-b">175 L</td></tr>
      <tr class="bg-bakery-cream"><td class="p-3 border-b">Manual 3-bay sink (per equivalent batch)</td><td class="p-3 border-b">15–25</td><td class="p-3 border-b">750–1,250 L</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2 class="mt-8 mb-3">Why Manual Washing Uses So Much More</h2>
  <p>A 3-bay sink uses 60–100 L per fill (depending on sink size). Even if you refill only twice a day, that's 120–200 L. Add the constant tap-running for rinsing and the per-item water consumption climbs to 3–8 L per item — far higher than any commercial dishwasher.</p>

  <h2 class="mt-8 mb-3">Annual Water Cost Impact</h2>
  <p>For a typical small bakery running 50 cycles/day, 300 days/year:</p>
  <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 mt-3">
    <li>JD-3: 37,500 L/year</li>
    <li>Hobart AMX: 57,000 L/year</li>
    <li>Manual sink: ~225,000 L/year</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="mt-3">At average commercial water+sewer rates of $4.50 per 1000 L (US/EU averages):</p>
  <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 mt-3">
    <li>JD-3: $168/year</li>
    <li>Hobart AMX: $256/year</li>
    <li>Manual sink: $1,012/year</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="mt-8 mb-3">How JD-3 Achieves Lower Water Consumption</h2>
  <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 mt-3">
    <li><strong>Precision rinse manifold:</strong> Engineered for minimum water volume to achieve coverage, not legacy over-rinsing.</li>
    <li><strong>Wash tank reuse:</strong> The wash tank water is recirculated for many cycles, filtered between uses. Only the rinse water is fresh-per-cycle.</li>
    <li><strong>Heat recovery option:</strong> Pre-warms incoming cold water, reducing the volume of "let it run until hot" that operators do.</li>
    <li><strong>Sealed door:</strong> Steam capture means less water evaporates from the wash tank per cycle (less refill needed).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="mt-8 mb-3">Sustainability Reporting</h2>
  <p>If your operation reports to ESG standards (typical for hotel groups, corporate cafeterias, large chains), JD-3 consumption data can be incorporated into your scope-3 reporting. We provide per-cycle measured consumption data sheets that meet most reporting frameworks.</p>

  <h2 class="mt-8 mb-3">In Water-Stressed Regions</h2>
  <p>For operations in Dubai, Riyadh, Cape Town, Las Vegas, Phoenix, southern California, or other water-scarce regions, the difference between 2.5 L/cycle and 4.0 L/cycle is significant — both in utility cost and in regulatory compliance. Some municipalities impose surcharges on commercial water use above benchmarks. JD-3's consumption typically falls below those benchmarks.</p>
</GuideLayout>
